# ARK Customer Classification Authority

ARK has four classification layers. Do not collapse them.

## Financial Authority Chain

```
Billing Class (customer)
        ↓
Default Scope Billing (new concerns)
        ↓
Scope Billing Posture (per concern)  ← FINANCIAL AUTHORITY
        ↓
Estimate Math
```

Scope billing posture is authoritative for fees, parts matrix, labor defaults, and discount eligibility per concern. Billing class only sets defaults.

## Layer Definitions

### Billing Class (`customers.customer_type`)

- **What:** Customer identity for billing — Retail, Fleet, Warranty, RepairPal, Internal, Wholesale, Comeback (+ legacy Business, Military).
- **UI label:** Billing Class (never "Customer tag" or "Customer type" in product copy).
- **Drives:** Default concern billing posture, standing discounts, document terms/disclaimers, labor category defaults.
- **Does not drive:** Per-scope fees/matrix after billing posture is set; marketing attribution; visit channel.

Primary billing classes for intake: Retail, Fleet, Warranty, RepairPal, Internal, Wholesale, Comeback.

**RepairPal** is a billing class when program rules apply ($150 labor, program parts profile, compliance) — not referral-only.

**Comeback** is a billing class for shop-warranty rework at $0 labor (distinct from Courtesy labor category on retail scopes).

### Referral Source (`customers.referral_source`)

- **What:** Marketing attribution — how the customer first found the shop (Google, Walk-in, RepairPal, etc.).
- **Drives:** Nothing operationally. Historical attribution only. Never default scope billing.
- **Set:** Intake customer create/edit. Independent of billing class.
- **Display:** Customer hub, RO identity header — read-only when populated.

Valid combinations:
- Billing Class = RepairPal, Referral = Google
- Billing Class = Retail, Referral = RepairPal

### Visit Source (`encounters.source`)

- **What:** How this specific visit arrived today (walk-in, phone, tow, etc.).
- **Drives:** Queue/intake card label only. Not billing.

### Scope Billing (`repair_order_concerns.billing_posture`)

- **What:** Financial authority per concern — Default, Customer pay, Fleet, Warranty, RepairPal, Internal, Wholesale, Comeback.
- **Drives:** Shop fees, parts matrix on new lines, labor defaults, standing discount eligibility.
- **Overrides:** Billing class defaults. Advisors set per scope on estimate.

## Implementation Discipline

- Do not drive estimate math or default scope billing from referral or visit source.
- Do not nest RepairPal under Warranty in product copy or defaults.
- Changing billing class at intake updates the customer profile and seeds new concern defaults.
- Changing billing class on customer does not retroactively change existing concern billing postures on open ROs.
- Document snapshots freeze billing-class disclaimers at generation time.
